# ISDN: The Digital Difference.

**Authors:** Piedmo, Greg

## Abstract
Integrated services digital network (ISDN) is a dial-up digital transmission service supporting transmission of audio, video, and text data over standard copper telephone wires or fiber optic cables. Advantages of ISDN over analog transmission include the ability of one phone line to support up to three simultaneous, separate conversations (phone, fax, computer), and increases in clarity and speed. (JKP)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ518479

